# Pirate portrait card frame

Read [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md) § "Collectable pirate portrait card frame".

**Quick rules:**

- Frames are WebP overlays: `public/images/cards/pirate-card-overlay1.webp` … `overlay7.webp` (`CARD_OVERLAYS` in `pirate-card.js`); sources in `images/cards-originals/`
- Regenerate: `npm run generate-card-overlay` (OpenAI `gpt-image-1`, prompt in `scripts/generate-card-overlay.js`, style from [aesthetic-style-guide.md](../aesthetic-style-guide.md))
- Card ratio **63:88**. Centre of PNG must stay transparent for the portrait; names are **HTML** in `.pirate-card__label`, not in the image.
- Render cards via `pirateCardHtml()` — do not duplicate markup.
- Portraits: `/images/portraits/<pirate_name_id>.jpg`
- Per-frame photo inset and label position: only in `pirate-card.css` (layout block). Tune via `/framefix` or `npm run detect-card-frame-layouts`.
- Do not replace with hand-drawn SVG unless user explicitly requests it.
